  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "On San Cha Mountain, Tyrant Heng Mei warns the Ten Tyrants not to pick a fight with Hu Mei Er. He says she seduces men to their death, has a wide network, is involved with Lin San Chi, has rumors with Li Xian, and even with Mo Wu Tian. Those three are all rank four Gu Masters. Li Xian is not a Southern Border native but came from Eastern Sea, an unscrupulous merchant famous among the demonic path members, skilled at buying low and selling high, with wide network and relationships.",
      "chapters": [
        339
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_san_cha_mountain",
        "char_tyrant_heng_mei",
        "fac_ten_tyrants",
        "char_hu_mei_er",
        "char_lin_san_chi",
        "char_mo_wu_tian",
        "fac_gu_masters",
        "reg_southern_border",
        "reg_eastern_sea"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He is short and fat. He has a round nose, large eyes, and a wide forehead. His hair lets out a greasy shine. One of his hands is short and rough.",
      "chapters": [
        344
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He is short and fat, with a round nose, large eyes, a wide forehead, and greasy hair. He is rank four upper stage, rarely fights, and makes a living by doing business with wide connections. Hu Mei Er presses him to move against Fang Yuan as little beast king. Alone afterward, he reads that request as her trying to use him, says he never does unprofitable business, and plans to befriend little beast king while watching others fight instead.",
      "chapters": [
        344
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "alone-after-the-visit",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan comes to deal. Li Xian serves tea with Eastern Sea blue sky Gu, a worm he often uses to impress Southern Border Gu Masters who do not know it. Fang Yuan offers Gu taken from King Quan Inheritance; Li Xian first offers one hundred and twenty rank three gold eating flying ant Gu in exchange. Fang Yuan instead hands him a list of Gu worms and refining materials that Li Xian reads as strength path needs. Li Xian says he cannot produce everything quickly and that the total price exceeds the Gu Fang Yuan offered; Fang Yuan asks him to supply what he has now and watch for the rest. Li Xian nods and agrees.",
      "chapters": [
        353
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "cave-tea-and-the-list",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_blue_sky_gu",
        "inh_king_quan_inheritance",
        "sys_gu_worms"
      ]
    }
  ],
